00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:53,170
Take that!

261
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,100
Come on!

262
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:57,040
Here we go!

263
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:58,760
With gusto!

264
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:06,996
They said it was cigarette poisoning.

265
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:09,420
The poor thing was still so young.

266
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:11,016
Here's what I heard.

267
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:12,159
See that bald guy?

268
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:16,307
Apparently a cigarette got mixed
into the mochi he was making.

269
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:24,080
Hurry up.

270
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,965
It's time to pound some mochi.

271
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:29,700
Am I in a time loop?

272
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:36,300
It's time to pound some mochi.

273
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:48,640
Pound the mochi.

274
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,980
I don't know why it's happening,

275
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:56,040
but I keep repeating the day
of the mochi pounding, and...

276
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:58,590
Amigo!

277
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:01,140
Someone dies every time.

278
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:05,900
Each day starts off the same way.

279
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,240
Let's pound the mochi!

280
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:12,045
I don't know how to escape
from this time loop.

281
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:17,420
However, if I can just finish this mochi
pounding peacefully without anyone dying,

282
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:19,457
then maybe...

283
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:22,320
The weather is awesome for New Year's Day.

284
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:24,380
Perfect for making mochi.

285
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:27,129
The landlord seems a
little bit sad though.

286
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:28,617
So when do we get to eat this stuff?

287
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:29,530
Up until now.

288
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:30,910
Confine!

289
00:18:30,993 --> 00:18:34,759
Whenever they got close to the
mortar, a fatal accident would happen.

290
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:36,320
Very well.

291
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:40,756
I just need to do something crazy
enough to keep them all away from it.

292
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:45,240
What the hell are you doing?

293
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:48,228
This going balls out,
couple with the mochi.

294
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:51,931
That being stomped around like
a fiddled fish out of water.

295
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:54,344
They should keep everyone away.

296
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:55,790
Huh?

297
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:58,614
No, the cannon's things are kicking in.

298
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,426
Daddy, don't touch it inside.

299
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:02,680
Don't come any closer!

300
00:19:05,660 --> 00:19:07,220
Oh, Johnny, no!

301
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:10,080
He's all strikes and no balls! It's done!

302
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,520
Eat it!

303
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:20,617
It was both soft and
high at the same time.

304
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:21,530
The loop didn't start over.

305
00:19:21,613 --> 00:19:22,480
Has it ended?

306
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:26,560
Am I the only one that knows
about this loop of fate?

307
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:30,000
You're Otani, right?

308
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,800
We just received a report.

309
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:35,039
Please come with us to the station.

310
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:48,960
It was the right thing to do.

311
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:54,121
Chainsmoker cat?

312
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,600
Rise and shine!

313
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:03,135
I thought we'd go get some
Awachi Island burgers today!

314
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:05,500
It's the new year.

315
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:07,209
Can't we just relax a bit?

316
00:20:08,020 --> 00:20:09,377
Relaxing was before eight.

317
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:10,397
It's time to get up!

318
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:13,437
And unless you plan on freezing
to death, we need more kerosene.

319
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:14,577
Quit lollygagging!

320
00:20:14,660 --> 00:20:15,580
Go and get it!

321
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,520
Gosh, that's such a pain.

322
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:19,308
Hands off, you dung beetle!

323
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:22,540
Oh, for crying out loud!

324
00:20:22,780 --> 00:20:23,900
No one's moving!

325
00:20:24,620 --> 00:20:25,757
Traffic on a holiday.

326
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:28,620
I swear, I'll tear all
these people a new one!

327
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:31,160
See how much mom loves traffic.

328
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:34,120
She sure is loud with her love. You know,

329
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:37,717
ever since you started living in that
apartment, you've been acting more like her.

330
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,677
Take that back or a whoopper ass!

331
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:41,054
Shut your damn mouths!

332
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:44,597
Oh, well, we haven't moved
an inch and I'm starving.

333
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:45,557
We're going home.

334
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,470
Seriously?

335
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:50,332
Here's your homemade Awaji Eileen Berger.

336
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:53,557
There's nothing better than being at home.

337
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:56,464
You realize you're the
one who wanted to go out.

338
00:20:57,860 --> 00:20:58,690
Um...

339
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:02,556
Kaoruko, did you put on a
few pounds over the holidays?

340
00:21:03,740 --> 00:21:05,697
You want my old maternity clothes?

341
00:21:05,780 --> 00:21:06,900
I'm not that big.

342
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:09,540
Do you want them, Shunran? Why would I?

343
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:12,857
Oh, you do kind of have
a big butt, though, sis.

344
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:14,857
If you wear those clothes backwards,

345
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:18,116
the part that's for the belly
will fit over your butt.

346
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:21,476
Thanks for the food.

347
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,757
There's more burgers if you want.

348
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:24,980
No, thanks.

349
00:21:25,260 --> 00:21:26,436
I'm a cow, remember?

350
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:27,500
I'm done, too.

351
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:32,777
You're not going anywhere!

352
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:34,684
After we eat, it's family time!

353
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:35,900
Are you crazy?

354
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:39,757
Why don't we all play a board game
together and watch Shinkigeki?

355
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:40,680
Oh, no.

356
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:44,817
We haven't been back home in a good
while, so Mom's all needy, isn't she?

357
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:47,060
Okay, I have an idea. You do?

358
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:53,157
I've been working on my beatboxing.

359
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,957
I don't give a real sense about that.

360
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,597
Now, if you lose, that means
you got to stay longer.

361
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:58,510
Hooray!

362
00:21:58,593 --> 00:21:59,423
Let's get this going.

363
00:21:59,506 --> 00:22:01,117
I've done some things, darling.

364
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:04,020
I'm sick of this goddamn house.

365
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:07,180
Boom, boom, hello. I'm Soonron.

366
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:32,057
See you

367
00:22:32,140 --> 00:22:37,400
next time.

368
00:23:23,733 --> 00:23:25,240
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

369
00:23:53,540 --> 00:23:54,370
Thank you.

370
00:24:23,540 --> 00:24:24,370
Thank you.

371
00:24:56,600 --> 00:24:57,880
Thank you.
